    {
      "name": "Multi-Agent Coordination",
      "summary": "Today's papers heavily feature advancements in the coordination of multi-agent systems, focusing on improving task performance in dynamic and challenging environments. For example, FedAgentKE ([2607.21361]) presents a federated framework that enhances knowledge transfer among agents, while Clustered Edge Intelligence ([2607.20937]) proposes a new perspective on edge computing and multi-agent collaborations. This theme reflects a strong interest in enhancing cooperation within AI systems, particularly in critical applications such as economic theory development and security protocols.",
